  "narrative": "All returned estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the corresponding claim and negative signed values favor the opposite direction. I used approximate clinical-magnitude thresholds based on 10% of the absolute mean dependency scale: SMARCA2 about 0.042, USP7 about 0.018, WRN about 0.030, KIF18A/POLR2A about 0.026, STAT3 about 0.028, and KRAS about 0.025. The SMARCA4-loss association with stronger SMARCA2 dependency remains decisive: in the combined high screen ROC and high Cas9 stratum it is +0.801 with a lower bound of +0.762, and it remains essentially as large in both highly aneuploid and less aneuploid lines, +0.759 and +0.798 respectively, with lower bounds far above the clinical threshold. These results argue against an explanation in which the SMARCA4-loss effect is merely a proxy for poor screen quality, poor editing, or extreme aneuploidy. I therefore accept H72-H74, keep H5 accepted, and close H5 as a sufficiently robust within-dataset association. The TP53-loss association with weaker USP7 dependency is also confirmed in the cleanest double high-quality stratum, +0.439 with lower bound +0.318, so H75 is accepted and closed. The USP7 lineage interaction is not informative: the signed point estimate is small and opposite, and the interval is very wide, so H76 is deferred rather than used to infer adenocarcinoma-specificity. The WRN MSI-high lineage interaction is similarly uninformative for the already validated H9 claim, with a small uncertain signed estimate, so H77 is deferred. The MSI specificity probes against KIF18A and POLR2A show no meaningful association, with estimates near zero; however their intervals are not tight enough to make a definitive negative statement, so H78 and H79 are left unresolved but deferred. The most important new finding is H80: among high-screen-ROC lines, PTEN loss is associated with markedly stronger STAT3 dependency, signed estimate +0.239 and interval +0.173 to +0.306. This is far above the approximate STAT3 10% threshold and is unlikely to be a simple noise signal, but it is new and was discovered in a stratum selected for screen quality, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association while keeping it active and requesting independent validation. PIK3CA mutation does not support stronger STAT3 dependency: the signed estimate is negative and the positive-side upper bound is below the STAT3 clinical threshold, so H81 is rejected and closed. PTEN loss among KRAS-mutant high-screen-ROC lines gives a potentially interesting positive signal for weaker KRAS dependency, but the exposed cell count is only 31 and the interval crosses null and is broad, so H82 is unresolved and deferred. RB1 loss versus KIF18A dependency is below the clinical threshold and uncertain, so H83 is unresolved and deferred.",
  "research_notes": "Updated dataset-specific conclusions: accepted and closed SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H5, H19, H31, H44, H51, H55, H61, H72, H73, H74; robust across high ROC/high Cas9 and aneuploidy strata). Accepted/closed/validated TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency (H8 plus H32, H56, H62, H75). Accepted/closed/validated MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency (H9 plus H25, H33, H42, H54, H57). Accepted/closed/validated KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H22 plus H29, H34, H53, H58). New accepted active claim H80: PTEN loss -> much stronger STAT3 dependency among high screen ROC; validation requested because it is large but new and stratum-selected. Rejected/specificity: H81 PIK3CA mutation -> stronger STAT3 dependency; H67 TP53-MDM2; H68 SMARCA4-POLR2A; H43 ARID1A effect; H2 BRAF; H6 canonical KEAP1; H10-H12 MYC effects; H16 KRAS-RIT1; H64 original NF1 direction. Unresolved/deferred or active low-confidence signals: H70/H71 high-quality KRAS/NF1 refinements, H69 post hoc NF1-loss weaker KRAS, H65 KRAS high Cas9, H82 PTEN among KRAS-mutant KRAS dependency, H83 RB1-KIF18A, H76 USP7 lineage interaction, H77 WRN lineage interaction, H78/H79 MSI specificity on KIF18A/POLR2A. Next priorities: await H80 validation; if confirmed, consider closing after PTEN-STAT3 full-population/high-Cas9/PIK3CA-wildtype/adenocarcinoma refinements; run H70/H71 next to resolve KRAS/NF1 and KRAS-mutation signals; avoid accepting H82/H83 until replication or stronger stratum evidence. Continue treating all claims as within-dataset associations, not causal or externally generalizable.",
